<http://data.silknow.org/object/827a6a65-8be9-3253-b024-ad32b30bca07>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Seal bag of crimson silk velvet, lined with red linen. It is circular in shape with a wide circular base reinforced with pasteboard and shallow sides pleated and pulled together with drawstrings.  The bag is couched with silver wire and filé; on the base is a coat-of-arms with 3 fleur-de-lys.  The drawstrings are finger-looped braids of crimson silk thread and silver filé, with 2 wooden tassel cores (once thread-covered)."@en , "Seal bag of crimson silk velvet, 1600s, French; silver embroidery with coat of arms"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/6eeecc93-c024-3d66-9c47-625e72cf8a1a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/44fbfc5e-cadc-3070-9dfb-243da041cb4d> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Seal bag of crimson silk velvet, 1600s, French; silver embroidery with coat of arms"@en , "Seal bag of crimson silk velvet, lined with red linen. It is circular in shape with a wide circular base reinforced with pasteboard and shallow sides pleated and pulled together with drawstrings.  The bag is couched with silver wire and filé; on the base is a coat-of-arms with 3 fleur-de-lys.  The drawstrings are finger-looped braids of crimson silk thread and silver filé, with 2 wooden tassel cores (once thread-covered)."@en ;
